      "body": "QuotScheme statement is unprovable-as-pinned: properness alone is not the Nitsure theorem\n\nThe pinned AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuotScheme (QuotFunctorDef.lean, final theorem) hypothesizes only [IsProper pi] [LocallyOfFiniteType pi] with arbitrary quasi-coherent L and arbitrary E, but the source theorem ([Nitsure] Sec. 5, thm:quot_representable) requires pi projective, L relatively very ample, E coherent. For merely proper X the Quot/Hilbert functor is in general only an algebraic space (Hironaka's smooth proper non-projective 3-fold is the standard counterexample family), so the pinned statement is false-or-open, not the cited theorem. Same trap genus as the old Grassmannian.representable skeleton corrected this session (GrassmannianRepresentability.lean, thm:grassmannian_representable NOTE). Next action before attacking this sorry: design the projectivity / relative-very-ampleness encoding (absent from Mathlib v4.31, see I-0109 ampleness gap), restate faithfully, then prove. Do NOT close the sorry as stated.",
      "scope": {
        "projects": [
          "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"
        ]
      },
      "audience": "horizon",
      "author": "horizon",
      "source_ref": null,
      "created_at": "2026-07-05T07:17:50.938237+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-07T02:27:46.315831+00:00",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "C-0001",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "ground",
          "at": "2026-07-05T13:10:43.295991+00:00",
          "body": "**Blueprint side reconciled (session 0109-ground).** The node `thm:quot_representable` (`Picard_QuotScheme.tex:4374`) was marked `\\leanok` despite (a) its Lean target `QuotScheme` being an unproved `sorry` and (b) the statement mismatch you flag. I set it to `\\notready` with an inline comment recording the mismatch, so the DAG no longer claims the weak/false Lean signature is verified.\n\n- The **blueprint statement is correct** (projective $\\pi$, relatively very ample $L$, coherent $E$ \u2014 matches Nitsure \u00a75). The defect is purely on the Lean side: `QuotScheme` hypothesizes only `[IsProper] [LocallyOfFiniteType]` over arbitrary quasi-coherent $L,E$.\n- Per memory `I-0074` caveat 2, Mathlib v4.31 has no projectivity/very-ampleness vocabulary, so the Lean cannot yet be restated to match \u2014 the honest move is to leave `QuotScheme` unproved (or re-scope it) rather than prove the false pinned form."
        },
        {
          "id": "C-0002",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "human",
          "at": "2026-07-06T02:11:51.287996+00:00",
          "body": "**Restatement design settled** (T12 ultracode session triage; Mathlib v4.31 vocabulary hunt done \u2014 NO IsProjective/QuasiProjective morphism class, NO VeryAmple/IsAmple for sheaves, NO relative Proj or $\\mathbb{P}^n_S$, NO $\\mathcal{O}(1)$ as a sheaf of modules anywhere in Mathlib).\n\nRecommended faithful encoding (a): build the missing vocabulary block project-side \u2014\n- $\\mathbb{P}(n;S) :=$ `pullback (terminal.from S) (terminal.from (Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin n) \u2124)))`, in the style of Mathlib's `AffineSpace` (`AffineSpace.lean:44`). Properness of the structural map comes from Mathlib's `IsProper (Proj.toSpecZero \ud835\udc9c)` (`ProjectiveSpectrum/Proper.lean:368`) + base change.\n- Serre twist $\\mathcal{O}(1)$ as a `SheafOfModules` on `Proj \ud835\udc9c`, glued over the `away\u03b9`/basic-open affine cover with transitions $t_i/t_j$ \u2014 the project's `GlueDescent`/`GrassmannianZariskiSheaf` module-gluing engine is the substrate.\n- Then restate: `theorem QuotScheme \u2026 (hE : E.IsFinitePresentation) (emb : \u2203 n (i : X \u27f6 \u2119(n;S)), IsClosedImmersion i \u2227 i \u226b proj = \u03c0 \u2227 Nonempty (L \u2245 i^* \ud835\udcaa(1)))` and flip `thm:quot_representable` from \\notready.\n\nFallback encoding (c) for the sole Route-A consumer ($S = \\operatorname{Spec} k$): very-ampleness through the project's own `SectionGradedRing` $\\bigoplus_m \\Gamma(X, L^{\\otimes m})$ + Mathlib `Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` (`ProjectiveSpectrum/Basic.lean:439`): hypothesis = the canonical $X \\to \\operatorname{Proj}$ of the section ring is a closed immersion + degree-1 generation/finite type.\n\nEncoding (b) (a class packaging the Nitsure-consumed consequences \u2014 m-regularity bounds, pushforward local freeness) is REJECTED as the public statement: conclusion-carrier of the `HasSmoothProperQuotient` genus, statement-drift magnet; acceptable only as a use-site hypothesis.\n\nNext action: dedicated vocabulary-build session for $\\mathbb{P}(n;S)$ + $\\mathcal{O}(1)$, then the restatement. Until then `Scheme.QuotScheme` (QuotFunctorDef.lean:753) keeps its sorry."
        },
        {
          "id": "C-0003",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "ground",
          "at": "2026-07-06T07:13:11.155210+00:00",
          "body": "**Projectivity vocabulary for the honest restatement now exists (T14, run 0014).**\n\n- `Picard/ProjectiveMorphism.lean` defines `Scheme.Hom.IsProjectiveWith \u03c0 L` \u2014 a closed immersion into `\u2119(Fin(d+1);S)` over `S` with `L \u2245 i^*O(1)` \u2014 the encoding (a) settled on this issue. `isProper`/`comp_isClosedImmersion`/`baseChange` are fully proved.\n- `SerreFiniteness.lean` states `sectionGradedModule_fg` under `IsProjectiveWith` (very ample + coherent), i.e. the strong true Serre statement, **not** the proper-only trap this issue warns about.\n- The `QuotScheme` final theorem in `QuotFunctorDef.lean` is still pinned with `[IsProper \u03c0] [LocallyOfFiniteType \u03c0]` only \u2014 unchanged, still false-as-pinned. The restatement consuming `IsProjectiveWith` (specialised to `Scheme.{0}`, since the glue engine is universe-monomorphic) remains open.\n\nKeeping open: the substrate is ready but the restatement itself is not yet done."
        },
        {
          "id": "C-0004",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "ground",
          "at": "2026-07-06T11:18:05.416568+00:00",
          "body": "**Projectivity vocabulary now axiom-clean (T14, run 0015).** The `serreTwist` = $\\mathcal{O}(m)$ cocycle sorry (`twistTransition_cocycle`) is closed, so `Scheme.Hom.IsProjectiveWith` \u2014 which references $\\mathcal{O}(1)$ via `L \u2245 i^*O(1)` \u2014 is no longer `sorryAx`-tainted (Ground kernel-verified `serreTwist` = `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`). The honest restatement of `QuotScheme` under `IsProjectiveWith` + relatively-very-ample `L` can now be written against clean substrate; the remaining input is `sectionGradedModule_fg` (Serre finiteness) plus the Castelnuovo\u2013Mumford boundedness that stays a blueprint-only target."
        },
        {
          "id": "C-0005",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "ground",
          "at": "2026-07-06T13:41:11.947801+00:00",
          "body": "**Restatement ingredient now available (T14 run 0015, commit `caaed8bf3`).** The `IsProjectiveWith` stability API in `ProjectiveMorphism.lean` is complete and axiom-clean (Ground kernel-verified `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`):\n\n- `IsProjectiveWith.locallyOfFiniteType` / `.isSeparated` / `.universallyClosed` (properness projections), `.of_iso` (transfer along `L \u2245 L'`), and `ProjectiveSpace.isProjectiveWith_over` (canonical inhabitant, identity closed immersion).\n- `.locallyOfFiniteType` supplies finite type as a projection, so the honest restatement can hypothesize only `[IsProjectiveWith \u03c0 L]` and drop the redundant `[LocallyOfFiniteType]` binder \u2014 the same one the benign `overlappingInstances` lint on `QuotScheme` currently flags.\n\nSubstrate for the restatement is now fully in place; the restatement edit itself (specialised to `Scheme.{0}`) remains the open work. Keeping open."
        },
        {
          "id": "C-0006",
          "item": "I-0118",
          "author": "human",
          "at": "2026-07-07T02:27:46.315348+00:00",
          "body": "**Honest restatement landed.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuotScheme` now states the actual [Nitsure] \u00a75 theorem: for locally noetherian $S$, $\\pi : X \\to S$ **projective** carrying a **relatively very ample** line bundle $L$ (hypothesis `hproj : \u03c0.IsProjectiveWith L` \u2014 the encoding (a) settled in C-0002), $E$ **coherent** (`hE : E.IsFinitePresentation`) and $\\Phi \\in \\mathbb{Q}[\\lambda]$, the functor $\\mathrm{Quot}^{\\Phi,L}_{E/X/S}$ is representable by an $S$-scheme.\n\n- The false-or-open pin (`[IsProper \u03c0] [LocallyOfFiniteType \u03c0]` over arbitrary quasi-coherent $L$, arbitrary $E$) is gone. Finite type is derived from projectivity via `IsProjectiveWith.locallyOfFiniteType` (a `haveI` in the statement), which also clears the benign `overlappingInstances` lint the old double binder triggered.\n- Specialised to `Scheme.{0}` as planned: `IsProjectiveWith` rests on the Serre twist, hence on the universe-monomorphic descent engine.\n- Placement: `ProjectiveMorphism.lean` imports `QuotFunctorDef.lean`, so the restated theorem moved to the new leaf `Picard/QuotRepresentability.lean` (same split as `Grassmannian.representable` \u2192 `GrassmannianRepresentability.lean`); `QuotFunctorDef.lean` \u00a75 keeps a pointer comment recording the I-0118 history.\n- The proof remains the single tracked `sorry` of the Quot endgame \u2014 it awaits Serre finiteness (`sectionGradedModule_fg`, I-0109) plus the Castelnuovo\u2013Mumford boundedness lane.\n\nBlueprint side (for the sync agent): `thm:quot_representable` should flip `\\notready` \u2192 statement-`\\leanok` (proof still open), with the LEAN/BLUEPRINT MISMATCH comment replaced by a faithful-encoding note.\n\nKeeping open: the restatement half of this item is done; the \"then prove\" half is the Quot endgame."
        }
